    "detailed_description": "Q: What should I do after entering the game?<br />\r\nAnswer: Try clicking on the grid. Be careful not to hit the mines.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQ: How do I know if a square is a mine?<br />\r\nAnswer: When you click on a grid, it will display a number indicating the number of mines within a 3*3 range. Based on these numbers you can calculate which tile has a mine.<br />\r\nOnce you determine that a grid is a mine, you can right-click on that grid to put a flag on that grid to remind yourself that it is a mine.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQuestion: What is a stone?<br />\r\nAnswer: Stones cannot be clicked. Nothing works, it just sits there quietly.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQ: What is sight distance?<br />\r\nAnswer: When you turn on sight range 2, the number displayed in the grid will be the number of 5*5 mines, not 3*3.<br />\r\nWhen you turn on sight distance 3, it will be 7*7.",
    "about_the_game": "Q: What should I do after entering the game?<br />\r\nAnswer: Try clicking on the grid. Be careful not to hit the mines.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQ: How do I know if a square is a mine?<br />\r\nAnswer: When you click on a grid, it will display a number indicating the number of mines within a 3*3 range. Based on these numbers you can calculate which tile has a mine.<br />\r\nOnce you determine that a grid is a mine, you can right-click on that grid to put a flag on that grid to remind yourself that it is a mine.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQuestion: What is a stone?<br />\r\nAnswer: Stones cannot be clicked. Nothing works, it just sits there quietly.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQ: What is sight distance?<br />\r\nAnswer: When you turn on sight range 2, the number displayed in the grid will be the number of 5*5 mines, not 3*3.<br />\r\nWhen you turn on sight distance 3, it will be 7*7.",
    "short_description": "On the basis of MineSweeper, sight range and stones are introduced to solve the dead-end situation of traditional MineSweeper. There are fifty levels from simple to difficult. In the fiftieth level, there are many grids of 6, 7, and 8, but there must be a solution. Global racing rankings.",
